{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rohanarun/sidorenko-template-refinements/pulls/2","id":4809332004,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVCWbLM8AAAABHqiVJA","html_url":"https://github.com/rohanarun/sidorenko-template-refinements/pull/2","diff_url":"https://github.com/rohanarun/sidorenko-template-refinements/pull/2.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/rohanarun/sidorenko-template-refinements/pull/2.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rohanarun/sidorenko-template-refinements/issues/2","number":2,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Cut the Sidorenko residual constant from 978 to 189 (even D ≥ 190)","user":{"login":"rohanarun","id":11659839,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNjU5ODM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11659839?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rohanarun","html_url":"https://github.com/rohanarun","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rohanarun/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rohanarun/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rohanarun/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rohanarun/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rohanarun/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rohanarun/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rohanarun/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rohanarun/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rohanarun/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Result\n\nThe nondirect residual contribution in OpenAI's *Costs for the remaining profiles* lemma is now bounded by $O_D(q^{-D+189})$, so even dimension **190** suffices for this one counting step — down from 980 (PR #1), 1034 (initial draft) and 1642 (source).\n\n![progress](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rohanarun/sidorenko-template-refinements/refine/sequential-basis-count/charts/progress.png)\n\n## Method\n\nThe earlier bounds count the $m$ active pair spaces as free two-dimensional subspaces of the global span. The paper's own **direct-case** count is sharper: it places one basis vector at a time, and each new vector must be symplectically orthogonal to everything already placed at either endpoint. This PR runs that count for the nondirect case too:\n\n- each basis vector records whether it raises the global span and whether it raises each endpoint span (type $(g,\\ell_i,\\ell_j)$, with $\\ell\\ge g$);\n- the defect $d=\\sum_i k_i-2k$ is exactly the number of vectors that raise a local span without raising the global one;\n- the identity $\\sum_i\\binom{k_i}{2}=\\sum_x\\sum_{\\ell=1}v'_i(x)$ cancels the containment cross terms, leaving $R=-2m+\\sum\\pi_x+(\\text{defect terms})$ where $\\pi_x$ is the overlap of the two endpoint spans;\n- averaging $\\pi\\le\\tfrac12(v'_i+v'_j)$ per vertex and using concavity gives $R\\le\\sum_i\\deg(i)^2-3m+\\lfloor(k_i+k_j-1)/2\\rfloor=262-84+11=189$ for $d=1$, and $R/d\\le122$ for $d\\ge2$.\n\nIn the direct case the same accounting reproduces the paper's exact exponent $-m$, which is a useful consistency check.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `audit_sequential.py` (standard library) reconstructs the allowed graph from the saved faces and cut bits, checks connectivity and the per-vertex concavity bound at every integer, exhausts all 8,192 supports and 55,173 relaxed defect-one strata with an integer convolution confirmed by an independent marginal-gain allocation, and checks the higher-defect ratio. Maximum: **189**, attained only on the full support with every local dimension at or one below full rank (spans 49–55), matching the closed form.\n- The combinatorial identities were also checked on random dependent subspace families over GF(3) (not included; the audit is exact and self-contained).\n- `python -B run_checks.py` passes locally end to end (plantri rebuild, enumeration, all earlier certificates, and the new audit); it is wired into CI.\n- `proof.tex` gains a section with the full argument and compiles (tectonic).\n\n## Scope\n\nOnly this one counting step is lowered. The earlier residue and transverse thresholds of the full construction remain required and may dominate. This is an AI-generated research draft; mathematical priority and formal verification are not claimed. `progress.md` has the timeline and a tweet draft.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","created_at":"2026-10-10T06:42:11Z","updated_at":"2026-10-10T12:41:40Z","closed_at":"2026-10-10T12:41:39Z","merged_at":"2026-10-10T12:41:39Z","merge_commit_sha":"d1df2a5cc0cb0c9003466b1c7f8ecb77a8e72a7d","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rohanarun/sidorenko-template-refinements/pulls/2/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rohanarun/sidorenko-template-refinements/pulls/2/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rohanarun/sidorenko-template-refinements/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rohanarun/sidorenko-template-refinements/issues/2/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rohanarun/sidorenko-template-refinements/statuses/b513fb4576b30443d0f41df556d378b676723e06","head":{"label":"rohanarun:refine/sequential-basis-count","ref":"refine/sequential-basis-count","sha":"b513fb4576b30443d0f41df556d378b676723e06","user":{"login":"rohanarun","id":11659839,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNjU5ODM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11659839?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rohanarun","html_url":"https://github.com/rohanarun","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rohanarun/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rohanarun/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rohanarun/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rohanarun/star